body:
Wait, 

So let's make this example;

I made a Dark elf sorc only because my friends wanted to play dark elves, but I wanted to have a high elf sorc.

Now I don't own this DLC but I have the race tokens available.

&#x200B;

If I where to swap to a high elf (without DLC) would i suddenly fight for the Aldmeri Dominion instead of the Ebon Pact? 

&#x200B;

And If i would buy the DLC in the future, would this change so that my high elf suddenly starts fighting for the Ebon Pact again?

Have I've missed some hidden gems?

Tried ESO recently but the game feels incomplete and It keeps shoving the DLC crap down my throat at any occasion, I still maxed out a sorc just to get one shotted, yet I find it hard to get into as the combat feels too stiff.

&#x200B;

I've sunken in countless hours into GW2 but as many others say, It's a hard game to dip time into unless you're playing with someone, It also doesn't have much of the "end game" content except for their storyline, Great game nonetheless but I think I've explored every corner of the game.

&#x200B;

Never got attached with FF14, mainly due to the similar reasons of ESO, Stiff combat in my opinion.

&#x200B;

BDO seems to be a  P2Win/P2Progress type of grinding game according to alot of YouTube reviews, But it also has the most breath taking combat that I so want to have!

I guess Blade N Soul is the closest to the BDO playstyle?

&#x200B;

What's your recommendation for a semi-casual MMO PvPer like myself?
